# the COFF object model to and from the neutral object
#
# to_neutral reads a COFF object, regular or bigobj, into a neutral object
# through the naming rows, the relocation set of its machine and the facts
# below. what the neutral model has no field for travels in the object's
# facts, keyed by COFF, so nothing a file states is dropped and the
# conversion back gives a file that converts to the same neutral object. a
# header the conversion cannot carry, as COFF line numbers, an auxiliary
# record of a function definition, a block or a CLR token, or a virtual size
# or address in an object, is refused rather than dropped.
#
# every section but .drectve is a neutral section of its name, its kind as
# the classifier reads its characteristics and name, its flags the memory
# characteristics state, and its alignment the ALIGN field's, sixteen when it
# states none as the PE Format default has it. a section of uninitialized
# data is zero fill. the characteristics the conversion back does not derive
# from the kind, flags and alignment are a fact. the .drectve options are the
# object's directives. a section of IMAGE_SCN_LNK_COMDAT is a group of its
# own: its section definition's selection names the rule, the first symbol
# defined in it after the definition names the signature and takes the
# section's size as its own, and an associative section's group follows the
# section its definition names, which it depends on. garbage collection
# treats each section as lld-link does: a COMDAT section is kept when
# referenced, an associative one lives with its leader, and every other
# section is a root.
#
# the neutral symbols are the symbol records, auxiliary records aside, in
# order. an external symbol is global, defined, common when it is undefined
# with a value, which is the common block's size and its own, aligned as
# lld-link aligns it, and undefined otherwise. a static symbol is local, and
# one with a section definition names its section. a weak external is weak
# and undefined, its fallback the symbol its record names, searched for as
# its characteristic's row states. a file symbol names the source file its
# records spell. a function is a symbol of the function type, a symbol in a
# thread-local section names thread-local data, and any other symbol states
# no kind. a local symbol of another storage class and a symbol of another
# type keep it in a fact. a relocation's addend is read from the bytes it
# patches, as its row says, and a record whose symbol field holds a number,
# as the AMD64 PAIR does, refers to nothing and holds the number as its
# addend.
#
# from_neutral builds the object of a neutral object for its machine, every
# record in the order the neutral object holds it, a section definition
# written for each symbol that names its section and for a COMDAT section
# that has none, and the signature symbol of a COMDAT section written right
# after its definition. the line records are lowered to CodeView first.

